    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-14",
      "title": "Attackers use Crypto Exchange Names to Disguise Unauthorized Sessions on 100+ ScreenConnect Servers",
      "summary": "Attackers registered more than 2,200 fake guest sessions on over 100 self-hosted ScreenConnect servers, named after crypto exchanges such as KUCOIN-SRV and BACKUP-PROBIT, with crypto trading-desktop thumbnails. The sessions were added between November 3 and November 13, 2026, and were kept online through repeated reconnections every few minutes. The guest installer was publicly downloadable on at least one server, which enabled registration. Huntress found no malicious activity from the fake guests themselves, though the researchers consider a bait for technicians exploiting CVE-2026-84869 their leading hypothesis but have not observed it. MSPs should upgrade affected clients to 26.6.5 or later, verify unfamiliar sessions before joining, and preserve the session database before deleting fakes.",
      "completeness": "Low",
      "threats": [
        "Screenconnect_tool",
        "Sckit_tool"
      ],
      "geo": [
        "Egyptian"
