    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-14",
      "title": "Aur0ra – An Xray Reverse Tunnel Hidden Inside Explorer After a Teams Vishing Call",
      "summary": "Hexastrike attributed with high confidence a September 2026 intrusion at a German manufacturing group to the Aur0ra ransomware group or an affiliate. The attacker sent email bombs, then posed as IT support over Microsoft Teams using a sender that impersonated a real employee. The victim installed AnyDesk, and the operator captured the domain password through a fake security prompt and uploaded it with a network inventory to a Microsoft dev tunnel. The operator then installed an Xray-core reverse tunnel, side-loaded as a DLL into Explorer via a per-user COM hijack, that disguised its traffic as Google connections. Defenders should note that monitoring-only controls recorded the activity without stopping it, and that a firewall rule allowing direct outbound connections bypassed the proxy.",
      "completeness": "High",
